pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: a level crossing an order definition's database swap. The
% `setlvl` below is still in force when `def_order` installs its fresh scratch
% database, and the checker recorded `database.len()` at the level for every
% constraint added while it was installed -- the `def` constraint and the
% transitivity proof's lines, i.e. SCRATCH indices 1-4. `wiplvl` is refused
% inside the definition (`OrderDefinitionPlacement`), so it always resolves the
% recorded indices against the PROBLEM database: here it deleted formula
% constraints 1-4, which the proof never tagged. Every one of them is trivially
% rederivable, so even forced checked deletion discharged them without a word
% -- the mis-deletion was completely silent, and only the `e` checks below
% catch it ("Trying to access constraint with ID 1 that has already been
% deleted"). Level recording is now suspended while an order-definition
% subcontext is open (`checker.rs`); the definition's constraints need no level
% bookkeeping, since they are discarded wholesale when their block ends and no
% deletion rule can reach them.
%
% What the format grants: `setlvl` marks "all following constraints" and
% `wiplvl` deletes only constraints "marked with <level> or a greater number"
% (proof_format_overview.md). The one problem-database constraint added after
% the `setlvl` is the `pol` sum, so that is what this `wiplvl` owes deletion --
% `is_deleted` pins that the suspension did not simply stop level recording
% altogether. This proof must verify: rejected before the fix, accepted after.
f 6;
setlvl 1;
def_order simple
    vars
        left u1;
        right v1;
        aux;
    end;
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0;
    end;
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1;
        end;
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                pol -2 -3 + -1 +;
            qed : -1;
        qed;
    end;
end;
pol 1 2 +;
wiplvl 1;
e 1 x1 >= 0 : 1;
e 1 x2 >= 0 : 2;
e 1 x3 >= 0 : 3;
e 1 x4 >= 0 : 4;
is_deleted 1 x1 1 x2 >= 0 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
